    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter July 2nd with a high-ceiling lineup anchored by **Junior Caminero**, who earns today\u2019s elite projection of 77.36. Batting in the #3 spot against Kolek, **Junior Caminero** benefits from a favorable wind projection and strong underlying xwOBA, positioning him as our primary source of run production. **Trea Turner** (66.78) and **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16) round out our top-tier plays; **Trea Turner** remains locked in at the leadoff spot where his stolen base upside is prioritized, while **Lars Nootbaar** draws a prime matchup against a vulnerable Waldrep (7.82 xERA), providing a massive boost to his efficiency score.\n\nWhile the majority of our outfield is positioned to capitalize on Waldrep\u2019s high xERA, **Nelson Velazquez** (58.67) and **Kyle Schwarber** (64.70) are tasked with driving in runs from the middle of the order. We are closely monitoring the lineup status for **Lars Nootbaar**, **Nelson Velazquez**, and **Junior Caminero**, as the shift in batting order could further amplify their projections. The most difficult personnel decision today was keeping **Dillon Dingler** (36.36) on the bench. Despite a solid 0.389 xwOBA, the combination of a difficult matchup against Eovaldi and a negative platoon split pushed him below our 40.0 efficiency floor, forcing us to prioritize the higher-upside profiles of **Colt Keith** and **Chase Meidroth** despite their own challenging SP matchups.\n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding **Colt Keith**, as he faces Eovaldi, an elite arm whose ability to neutralize base runners poses a specific threat to our stolen base efficiency goals. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** draws a tough assignment against Burns; while his dynamic platoon edge keeps his score at 55.42, he remains a candidate for early substitution if the game script turns unfavorable. We remain aggressive in the SB category, but with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Yordan Alvarez** idle due to scheduled off-days, our bench depth is intentionally thin, necessitating that our active starters deliver against their respective right-handed counterparts.",
